  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A static browser workbench (Arabic right-to-left interface with English engineering terms) that takes a drainage engineer from project identity and raw rainfall through to an Annual Maximum series, a Gumbel IDF table, a design intensity, SCS-CN runoff, design-storm hyetographs and Rational Method peak flow, then a results dashboard with CSV, PNG and project-file exports. It does not size conduits (no Manning or pipe design). Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
